{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You want a video that plays while it generates. You also want to change the prompt mid-run. A finite video job stops with a file. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateLiveVideo()"},{"type":"text","value":" opens a session instead."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateLiveVideo()"},{"type":"text","value":" on the server. It returns a connect payload: a model id, a prompt, and a token. The browser uses that payload to open the stream."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Experimental."}]},{"type":"text","value":" The API can change. Live models bill per session-second while a GPU is held."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"1-mint-a-session-on-the-server","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Mint a session on the server"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pick one adapter. They do not return a download URL."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateLiveVideo } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { reactorVideo } from '@tanstack/ai-reactor'\n\nconst live = await generateLiveVideo({\n  adapter: reactorVideo('helios'),\n  prompt: 'A chef tosses noodles in a steel wok, flames leaping',\n})\n\n// Hand live.token, live.model, and live.prompt to the browser.","lang":"ts","meta":"group=live-reactor"},{"type":"code","value":"import { generateLiveVideo } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { falLiveVideo } from '@tanstack/ai-fal'\n\nconst live = await generateLiveVideo({\n  adapter: falLiveVideo('minimax/h3-max/director'),\n  prompt: 'Live shopping stream: a host holds up a gold watch to camera',\n})\n\n// live.model is 'fal-ai/minimax-h3-max-director'. Hand it to the browser.","lang":"ts","meta":"group=live-fal"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"REACTOR_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FAL_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":", or pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"apiKey"},{"type":"text","value":" in the adapter config. Do not put the key in the JSON body."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A full app lives in "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/tree/main/examples/ts-react-media","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"examples/ts-react-media"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"2-connect-in-the-browser","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Connect in the browser"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The server half is the same for every live adapter. The browser client is not."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"reactor","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reactor"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@reactor-team/js-sdk"},{"type":"text","value":". Connect with the token. Helios uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"set_sr_scale"},{"type":"text","value":", then "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"set_prompt"},{"type":"text","value":", then "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"start"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Reactor } from '@reactor-team/js-sdk'\n\nconst reactor = new Reactor({ modelName: live.model })\nconst video = document.querySelector('video')\n\nreactor.on('trackReceived', (name, _track, stream) => {\n  if (name !== 'main_video') return\n  if (!video) return\n  video.muted = true\n  const attach = () => {\n    video.srcObject = null\n    video.srcObject = stream\n    void video.play().catch((error: unknown) => {\n      if (error instanceof DOMException && error.name === 'AbortError') return\n    })\n  }\n  attach()\n  for (const track of stream.getTracks()) {\n    track.addEventListener('unmute', attach)\n  }\n})\n\nawait reactor.connect(live.token)\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_sr_scale', { sr_scale: '2x' })\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_prompt', { prompt: live.prompt })\nawait reactor.sendCommand('start', {})","lang":"ts","meta":"group=live-reactor"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"FastH3 uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enqueue"},{"type":"text","value":" only. LongLive uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"set_shot"},{"type":"text","value":" then "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"start"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Helios can also take a seed image. Pass a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"File"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<input type=\"file\">"},{"type":"text","value":". Do not send base64."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const picker = document.querySelector('input[type=\"file\"]')\nif (!(picker instanceof HTMLInputElement)) {\n  throw new Error('Pick a seed image')\n}\nconst file = picker.files?.[0]\nif (file === undefined) {\n  throw new Error('Pick a seed image')\n}\nconst image = await reactor.uploadFile(file)\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_conditioning', { prompt: live.prompt, image })\nawait reactor.sendCommand('start', {})","lang":"ts","meta":"group=live-reactor"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A later "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"set_prompt"},{"type":"text","value":" morphs the shot at the next chunk."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/reactor","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reactor adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for model ids."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"fal-h3-max-director","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fal H3 Max Director"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@fal-ai/client@alpha"},{"type":"text","value":". Keep "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FAL_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":" on the server. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"live.model"},{"type":"text","value":" is the WMA app id. Open WMA through a proxy that attaches the key. Do not send "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"live.token"},{"type":"text","value":" as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Key"},{"type":"text","value":" credentials."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The example proxy is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/routes/api.fal.proxy.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" in "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/tree/main/examples/ts-react-media","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"examples/ts-react-media"}]},{"type":"text","value":". It attaches the key and forwards only to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"wma.fal.run"},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/ice"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/session"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/session/heartbeat"},{"type":"text","value":") and Director "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/ice"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createFalClient } from '@fal-ai/client'\nimport { wma } from '@fal-ai/client/realtime'\n\nconst fal = createFalClient({ proxyUrl: '/api/fal/proxy' })\nconst video = document.querySelector('video')\n\nconst session = fal.realtime.open(wma(live.model), {\n  receive: ['video', 'audio'],\n  onError: (error) => {\n    console.error(error)\n  },\n  onMedia: (stream) => {\n    if (!video) return\n    video.muted = true\n    video.srcObject = stream\n    void video.play().catch((error: unknown) => {\n      if (error instanceof DOMException && error.name === 'AbortError') return\n    })\n  },\n})\n\nsession.send({\n  type: 'configure',\n  prompt: live.prompt,\n  prompt_version: 1,\n  protocol_version: 1,\n})\n\nawait session.ready","lang":"ts","meta":"group=live-fal"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To steer, send "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ type: 'prompt', prompt, prompt_version }"},{"type":"text","value":" and increase "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prompt_version"},{"type":"text","value":" each time. To stop, send "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ type: 'stop' }"},{"type":"text","value":" and close the session."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Director bills a 60 second minimum. Resolution is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"480p"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"768p"},{"type":"text","value":". See the "},{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/fal","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fal adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"models","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Models"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adapter"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Id"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What it does"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reactorVideo()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"helios"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interactive realtime video"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reactorVideo()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fast-h3"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fast live clips on a live track"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reactorVideo()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"longlive-v2"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shot-based live clips"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"falLiveVideo()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"minimax/h3-max/director"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Steerable live stream over WMA"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For Orbis and LingBot, use "},{"type":"link","href":"./world-generation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"World Generation"}]},{"type":"text","value":". For a file that finishes, use "},{"type":"link","href":"./video-generation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Video Generation"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-you-have-now","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What you have now"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A server call that returns a connect payload. The browser opens the stream and steers it until you stop."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"1-mint-a-session-on-the-server","text":"1. Mint a session on the server","level":2},{"id":"2-connect-in-the-browser","text":"2. Connect in the browser","level":2},{"id":"reactor","text":"Reactor","level":3},{"id":"fal-h3-max-director","text":"fal H3 Max Director","level":3},{"id":"models","text":"Models","level":2},{"id":"what-you-have-now","text":"What you have now","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYou want a video that plays while it generates. You also want to change the prompt mid-run. A finite video job stops with a file. `generateLiveVideo()` opens a session instead.\n\nCall `generateLiveVideo()` on the server. It returns a connect payload: a model id, a prompt, and a token. The browser uses that payload to open the stream.\n\n> **Experimental.** The API can change. Live models bill per session-second while a GPU is held.\n\n## 1. Mint a session on the server\n\nPick one adapter. They do not return a download URL.\n\n```ts group=live-reactor\nimport { generateLiveVideo } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { reactorVideo } from '@tanstack/ai-reactor'\n\nconst live = await generateLiveVideo({\n  adapter: reactorVideo('helios'),\n  prompt: 'A chef tosses noodles in a steel wok, flames leaping',\n})\n\n// Hand live.token, live.model, and live.prompt to the browser.\n```\n\n```ts group=live-fal\nimport { generateLiveVideo } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { falLiveVideo } from '@tanstack/ai-fal'\n\nconst live = await generateLiveVideo({\n  adapter: falLiveVideo('minimax/h3-max/director'),\n  prompt: 'Live shopping stream: a host holds up a gold watch to camera',\n})\n\n// live.model is 'fal-ai/minimax-h3-max-director'. Hand it to the browser.\n```\n\nSet `REACTOR_API_KEY` or `FAL_KEY`, or pass `apiKey` in the adapter config. Do not put the key in the JSON body.\n\nA full app lives in [`examples/ts-react-media`](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/tree/main/examples/ts-react-media).\n\n## 2. Connect in the browser\n\nThe server half is the same for every live adapter. The browser client is not.\n\n### Reactor\n\nInstall `@reactor-team/js-sdk`. Connect with the token. Helios uses `set_sr_scale`, then `set_prompt`, then `start`.\n\n```ts group=live-reactor\nimport { Reactor } from '@reactor-team/js-sdk'\n\nconst reactor = new Reactor({ modelName: live.model })\nconst video = document.querySelector('video')\n\nreactor.on('trackReceived', (name, _track, stream) => {\n  if (name !== 'main_video') return\n  if (!video) return\n  video.muted = true\n  const attach = () => {\n    video.srcObject = null\n    video.srcObject = stream\n    void video.play().catch((error: unknown) => {\n      if (error instanceof DOMException && error.name === 'AbortError') return\n    })\n  }\n  attach()\n  for (const track of stream.getTracks()) {\n    track.addEventListener('unmute', attach)\n  }\n})\n\nawait reactor.connect(live.token)\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_sr_scale', { sr_scale: '2x' })\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_prompt', { prompt: live.prompt })\nawait reactor.sendCommand('start', {})\n```\n\nFastH3 uses `enqueue` only. LongLive uses `set_shot` then `start`.\n\nHelios can also take a seed image. Pass a `File` from `<input type=\"file\">`. Do not send base64.\n\n```ts group=live-reactor\nconst picker = document.querySelector('input[type=\"file\"]')\nif (!(picker instanceof HTMLInputElement)) {\n  throw new Error('Pick a seed image')\n}\nconst file = picker.files?.[0]\nif (file === undefined) {\n  throw new Error('Pick a seed image')\n}\nconst image = await reactor.uploadFile(file)\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_conditioning', { prompt: live.prompt, image })\nawait reactor.sendCommand('start', {})\n```\n\nA later `set_prompt` morphs the shot at the next chunk.\n\nSee the [Reactor adapter](../adapters/reactor) for model ids.\n\n### fal H3 Max Director\n\nInstall `@fal-ai/client@alpha`. Keep `FAL_KEY` on the server. `live.model` is the WMA app id. Open WMA through a proxy that attaches the key. Do not send `live.token` as `Key` credentials.\n\nThe example proxy is `src/routes/api.fal.proxy.ts` in [`examples/ts-react-media`](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/tree/main/examples/ts-react-media). It attaches the key and forwards only to `wma.fal.run` (`/ice`, `/session`, `/session/heartbeat`) and Director `/ice`.\n\n```ts group=live-fal\nimport { createFalClient } from '@fal-ai/client'\nimport { wma } from '@fal-ai/client/realtime'\n\nconst fal = createFalClient({ proxyUrl: '/api/fal/proxy' })\nconst video = document.querySelector('video')\n\nconst session = fal.realtime.open(wma(live.model), {\n  receive: ['video', 'audio'],\n  onError: (error) => {\n    console.error(error)\n  },\n  onMedia: (stream) => {\n    if (!video) return\n    video.muted = true\n    video.srcObject = stream\n    void video.play().catch((error: unknown) => {\n      if (error instanceof DOMException && error.name === 'AbortError') return\n    })\n  },\n})\n\nsession.send({\n  type: 'configure',\n  prompt: live.prompt,\n  prompt_version: 1,\n  protocol_version: 1,\n})\n\nawait session.ready\n```\n\nTo steer, send `{ type: 'prompt', prompt, prompt_version }` and increase `prompt_version` each time. To stop, send `{ type: 'stop' }` and close the session.\n\nDirector bills a 60 second minimum. Resolution is `480p` or `768p`. See the [fal adapter](../adapters/fal).\n\n## Models\n\n| Adapter | Id | What it does |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `reactorVideo()` | `helios` | Interactive realtime video |\n| `reactorVideo()` | `fast-h3` | Fast live clips on a live track |\n| `reactorVideo()` | `longlive-v2` | Shot-based live clips |\n| `falLiveVideo()` | `minimax/h3-max/director` | Steerable live stream over WMA |\n\nFor Orbis and LingBot, use [World Generation](./world-generation). For a file that finishes, use [Video Generation](./video-generation).\n\n## What you have now\n\nA server call that returns a connect payload. The browser opens the stream and steers it until you stop.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Live Generation\nid: live-generation\norder: 6.5\ndescription: \"Open a live, prompt-steerable video session with generateLiveVideo(). Mint a connect payload on the server, connect in the browser, and steer the stream with new prompts.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - live generation\n  - generateLiveVideo\n  - reactor\n  - fal\n  - h3 max director\n  - helios\n  - live video\n  - experimental\n---\n\nYou want a video that plays while it generates. You also want to change the prompt mid-run. A finite video job stops with a file. `generateLiveVideo()` opens a session instead.\n\nCall `generateLiveVideo()` on the server. It returns a connect payload: a model id, a prompt, and a token. The browser uses that payload to open the stream.\n\n> **Experimental.** The API can change. Live models bill per session-second while a GPU is held.\n\n## 1. Mint a session on the server\n\nPick one adapter. They do not return a download URL.\n\n```ts group=live-reactor\nimport { generateLiveVideo } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { reactorVideo } from '@tanstack/ai-reactor'\n\nconst live = await generateLiveVideo({\n  adapter: reactorVideo('helios'),\n  prompt: 'A chef tosses noodles in a steel wok, flames leaping',\n})\n\n// Hand live.token, live.model, and live.prompt to the browser.\n```\n\n```ts group=live-fal\nimport { generateLiveVideo } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { falLiveVideo } from '@tanstack/ai-fal'\n\nconst live = await generateLiveVideo({\n  adapter: falLiveVideo('minimax/h3-max/director'),\n  prompt: 'Live shopping stream: a host holds up a gold watch to camera',\n})\n\n// live.model is 'fal-ai/minimax-h3-max-director'. Hand it to the browser.\n```\n\nSet `REACTOR_API_KEY` or `FAL_KEY`, or pass `apiKey` in the adapter config. Do not put the key in the JSON body.\n\nA full app lives in [`examples/ts-react-media`](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/tree/main/examples/ts-react-media).\n\n## 2. Connect in the browser\n\nThe server half is the same for every live adapter. The browser client is not.\n\n### Reactor\n\nInstall `@reactor-team/js-sdk`. Connect with the token. Helios uses `set_sr_scale`, then `set_prompt`, then `start`.\n\n```ts group=live-reactor\nimport { Reactor } from '@reactor-team/js-sdk'\n\nconst reactor = new Reactor({ modelName: live.model })\nconst video = document.querySelector('video')\n\nreactor.on('trackReceived', (name, _track, stream) => {\n  if (name !== 'main_video') return\n  if (!video) return\n  video.muted = true\n  const attach = () => {\n    video.srcObject = null\n    video.srcObject = stream\n    void video.play().catch((error: unknown) => {\n      if (error instanceof DOMException && error.name === 'AbortError') return\n    })\n  }\n  attach()\n  for (const track of stream.getTracks()) {\n    track.addEventListener('unmute', attach)\n  }\n})\n\nawait reactor.connect(live.token)\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_sr_scale', { sr_scale: '2x' })\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_prompt', { prompt: live.prompt })\nawait reactor.sendCommand('start', {})\n```\n\nFastH3 uses `enqueue` only. LongLive uses `set_shot` then `start`.\n\nHelios can also take a seed image. Pass a `File` from `<input type=\"file\">`. Do not send base64.\n\n```ts group=live-reactor\nconst picker = document.querySelector('input[type=\"file\"]')\nif (!(picker instanceof HTMLInputElement)) {\n  throw new Error('Pick a seed image')\n}\nconst file = picker.files?.[0]\nif (file === undefined) {\n  throw new Error('Pick a seed image')\n}\nconst image = await reactor.uploadFile(file)\nawait reactor.sendCommand('set_conditioning', { prompt: live.prompt, image })\nawait reactor.sendCommand('start', {})\n```\n\nA later `set_prompt` morphs the shot at the next chunk.\n\nSee the [Reactor adapter](../adapters/reactor) for model ids.\n\n### fal H3 Max Director\n\nInstall `@fal-ai/client@alpha`. Keep `FAL_KEY` on the server. `live.model` is the WMA app id. Open WMA through a proxy that attaches the key. Do not send `live.token` as `Key` credentials.\n\nThe example proxy is `src/routes/api.fal.proxy.ts` in [`examples/ts-react-media`](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/tree/main/examples/ts-react-media). It attaches the key and forwards only to `wma.fal.run` (`/ice`, `/session`, `/session/heartbeat`) and Director `/ice`.\n\n```ts group=live-fal\nimport { createFalClient } from '@fal-ai/client'\nimport { wma } from '@fal-ai/client/realtime'\n\nconst fal = createFalClient({ proxyUrl: '/api/fal/proxy' })\nconst video = document.querySelector('video')\n\nconst session = fal.realtime.open(wma(live.model), {\n  receive: ['video', 'audio'],\n  onError: (error) => {\n    console.error(error)\n  },\n  onMedia: (stream) => {\n    if (!video) return\n    video.muted = true\n    video.srcObject = stream\n    void video.play().catch((error: unknown) => {\n      if (error instanceof DOMException && error.name === 'AbortError') return\n    })\n  },\n})\n\nsession.send({\n  type: 'configure',\n  prompt: live.prompt,\n  prompt_version: 1,\n  protocol_version: 1,\n})\n\nawait session.ready\n```\n\nTo steer, send `{ type: 'prompt', prompt, prompt_version }` and increase `prompt_version` each time. To stop, send `{ type: 'stop' }` and close the session.\n\nDirector bills a 60 second minimum. Resolution is `480p` or `768p`. See the [fal adapter](../adapters/fal).\n\n## Models\n\n| Adapter | Id | What it does |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `reactorVideo()` | `helios` | Interactive realtime video |\n| `reactorVideo()` | `fast-h3` | Fast live clips on a live track |\n| `reactorVideo()` | `longlive-v2` | Shot-based live clips |\n| `falLiveVideo()` | `minimax/h3-max/director` | Steerable live stream over WMA |\n\nFor Orbis and LingBot, use [World Generation](./world-generation). For a file that finishes, use [Video Generation](./video-generation).\n\n## What you have now\n\nA server call that returns a connect payload. The browser opens the stream and steers it until you stop.\n"}
